# LLM Integration Standards

## Architecture
- All LLM calls go through server-side Next.js Route Handlers (`src/app/api/`). Never call the OpenAI API from client components — the key must stay server-only.
- Use `getTracedOpenAIClient()` from `src/lib/llm/observability.ts` for direct calls, or `getInstructorClient()` from `src/lib/llm/instructor.ts` for structured output. `client.ts` exposes only `getModelName()` and `isReasoningModel()`.

## Prompt Engineering
- **Version every prompt.** Change `PROMPT_VERSION` in `src/lib/llm/prompts/rationale.ts` when the system prompt changes materially. Add a changelog entry.
- **Format data as markdown tables** using `src/lib/llm/formatters.ts` — structured tables dramatically improve LLM comprehension of numerical portfolio data.
- Keep temperature low (≤ 0.3) for financial content to reduce hallucination risk.
- Include chain-of-thought instructions ("consider X, then Y") in the system prompt for complex reasoning tasks.

## Guardrails
- **Always validate inputs** with `validateRationaleRequest()` from `guardrails.ts` before sending to the LLM.
- **Always normalise outputs** with `normalizeRationaleResponse()` from `guardrails.ts` — never pass raw LLM JSON to the UI.
- For standard models (GPT-4o), use Instructor + Zod via `getInstructorClient()` for structured output with automatic retries.
- Provide a graceful fallback (algorithmic rationale) when AI generation fails — never leave the user with a broken UI.

## Token Management
- Call `assertFitsContext(prompt, model)` before every LLM call to catch budget overruns early.
- Use `estimateTokens()` for pre-call budget checks; log `response.usage.total_tokens` post-call.

## Observability (Langfuse)
- Use `getTracedOpenAIClient()` from `src/lib/llm/observability.ts` — it wraps the base client with `observeOpenAI()` from `@langfuse/openai`.
- Langfuse is **opt-in** — set `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY` + `LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY` in `.env.local` to enable. Omit them to disable silently.
- Always include `promptVersion` in trace metadata so rollbacks are auditable.

## Reasoning (o-series) Models
- o1/o3/o4-mini do not support `temperature` or `response_format: json_object` on all API versions — use `isReasoningModel()` to gate these params.
- For structured JSON from reasoning models, instruct the model in the prompt: "Return ONLY a JSON object with no markdown fences."

## Security
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` must live only in `.env.local` (gitignored). Never hardcode it.
- Never log full prompt or response content in production — use Langfuse for observability instead.
- Rotate the API key immediately if it appears in source code, PR diffs, or chat logs.
